---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — The Oracles"
  description="How The Oracles and its internal tool, Oracles Social, handle data from our own YouTube, TikTok, Instagram and X accounts."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <section class="vhero">
    <h1 class="vhero__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="vhero__sub mono muted">Last updated: November 10, 2026</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="measure">
      <p class="lead">
        The Oracles (&ldquo;we&rdquo;) runs theoracles.studio and a small internal
        tool, Oracles Social, which publishes The Oracles&rsquo; own videos to our
        own social media accounts and reads how they perform.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        <strong>What the tool accesses.</strong> Oracles Social connects only to
        accounts The Oracles owns: our YouTube channel, our TikTok account, our
        Instagram account and our X account. An Oracles team member authorizes
        each connection. The tool may upload and schedule our own videos and their
        captions, read our posts&rsquo; performance numbers (such as views, likes,
        comments, shares, watch time and audience totals), and read and reply to
        comments on our own posts. It does not access any other person&rsquo;s
        account or data.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        <strong>How we use it.</strong> We use this information only to publish
        our own content and to measure how it performs. It is kept in our private
        records and is never sold, shared with third parties or used for
        advertising.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        <strong>Comments.</strong> When the tool reads comments on our posts, it
        sees what the commenter made public on that platform (their username and
        comment). We use it only to read and answer comments on our own posts.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        <strong>Google user data.</strong> Our use of information received from
        Google APIs follows the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
        including the Limited Use requirements. You can revoke the tool&rsquo;s
        access at any time at
        <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        <strong>TikTok.</strong> Our use of TikTok&rsquo;s APIs follows
        TikTok&rsquo;s developer terms. The connection can be removed at any time
        in TikTok&rsquo;s settings for authorized apps.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        <strong>This website.</strong> theoracles.studio does not require an
        account. If you email us, we use your message only to reply.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        <strong>Contact.</strong> Questions about this policy:
        <a href="mailto:hello@theoracles.studio">hello@theoracles.studio</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
